WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
Take two districts in England.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.330
In one, a third of the
people are 65 or over.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.270
In the other, it's about one in eighteen.

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:16.380
Meanwhile the whole UK keeps growing:
59.1 million people in mid-2001,

5
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:20.070
69.5 million by mid-2025.

6
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:26.140
Yet births in the year to mid-2025
were the lowest for at least 43 years.

7
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.470
So what makes one place so
old, and another so young?

8
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.410
In this mission, you'll pull
apart the UK's growth into births,

9
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.310
deaths and migration.

10
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.010
Then you'll weigh up what an ageing
population means for pensions,

11
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.830
care and housing.

12
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: find out
what makes a place old.
